            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0445" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/893: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-16"
                            >June 16, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received June 16—8:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2733. Exchange negotiations—Japan. Department’s 1536, June 15.<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d364-f1"/> Swiss Legation Tokyo telegraphs June 15 following.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“It is officially confirmed that departure of <hi rendition="#italic">Asama
                            Maru</hi> scheduled for Wednesday June 17. <hi rendition="#italic">Conte
                            Verde</hi> will leave Osaka June 18 for Shanghai where it will take
                        aboard officials and non-officials to be repatriated. Readjusting
                        distribution plan of cabins according to indications contained in your
                        telegram (Department’s 1499, June 10). Endeavoring arrange matters to avoid
                        any complaints of diplomats of other countries than United States, probably
                        cannot please everybody with such large number of passengers but will do
                        best to insure equitable distribution.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Confirm sailing date of <hi rendition="#italic">Asama Maru</hi> June 17 as
                    correct date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
